<p>Interested in completely free, browser-based, instructional logic software?<span id="more-57798"></span></p>
<p><a href="https://brianrabern.net/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Brian Rabern</a> spent a decade at the University of Edinburgh working in logic, formal semantics, and other areas of philosophy before moving into the tech world.</p>
<p>Unable to find logic software that met his needs, he and a former student created <a href="https://elogic.land/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><em>Elogic</em></a>. Initially developed for his courses, it has since been used at several universities.</p>
<p>He is now making the software freely available to anyone who wants to use it. He describes it below.</p>
